            <ArticleTitle>Myocardial infarction related to aberrant left circumflex artery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e51-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.ijcard.2008.06.067</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case of lateral wall infarction in the territory of an anomalous circumflex artery without significant stenosis. The unusual location of the infarction suggests a causal relation with the anomalous artery through minor plaque rupture, which may have resulted from mechanical stress.</AbstractText>
